## -*-makefile-*-
## HobbyOS bare-metal overlay -- NOT upstream ICU.  This file is committed
## at third_party/icu-78.3/config/mh-unknown and is copied over the vendored
## tree's src/source/config/mh-unknown by build-target.sh before every
## configure run (same overlay pattern as libcxx-21.1.8/config/__config_site).
##
## Why this file exists: ICU's configure maps --host=${arch}-none-elf to the
## platform fragment "mh-unknown", which upstream ships as a deliberate error
## stub ("*** ERROR - configure could not detect your platform").  ICU's own
## advice in that stub is "try copying icu/source/config/mh-linux to
## mh-unknown" -- this is exactly that copy.
##
## Bare-metal deltas vs upstream mh-linux: none in the fragment itself.
##   * LDFLAGSICUDT / THREADSCPPFLAGS are kept verbatim (cross-notes.md pins
##     them as the values the target build relies on).
##   * -ldl / -lpthread are NOT here in the first place: upstream gets them
##     from configure's LIBS at link time, and the HobbyOS target build
##     overrides LIBS with the in-tree sysroot (obj/<arch>/crt0.o +
##     obj/<arch>/libc.a), where HobbyOS pthreads live inside libc.a.
##   * the shared-library / soname / rpath rules below are inert under the
##     build's --disable-shared.
## Fragments are included last and may override anything; this one overrides
## nothing.  Full rationale + measured results: ../../cross-notes.md.
##
## Upstream text follows, verbatim (copied from src/source/config/mh-linux,
## sha256 548f780bb9caba18bfe613d4b8317f66ab0f07c58abfb7d9d6c0aa88c4fe9e74,
## ICU 78.3).
